# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, useless to it, or must
# never leave this machine. Without this file the build context also carries
# .framecast/ — which holds finished renders, currently ~175MB — to the
# builder on every single build.

# Dependencies and build output: reinstalled/regenerated in the image.
node_modules
.next
out
src/generated

# Finished renders and other local pipeline scratch.
.framecast

# Secrets. `.env.local` in particular holds the credential-encryption key and
# the provider keys. Runtime configuration is injected by the host, never
# baked into an image — and `worker/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .`, so anything
# not listed here really does end up in a published GHCR image.
# `*.env` covers the server-side family too (`deploy/prod.env`,
# `deploy/staging.env`, `deploy/backup.env`), which the runbook creates by
# copying a `.example` and filling it in — see .gitignore for the same split.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example

# Local-only tooling and history.
.git
.gitignore
.vercel
.superpowers
.claude
coverage
*.log

# Documentation and specs: not needed to run anything.
docs
README.md

# NOTE: `public/` is deliberately NOT ignored. This file applies to every
# build from this context, and the app's own Dockerfile copies public/ into
# its runtime image — excluding it here would break that build to save the
# worker a few kilobytes.
